[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite.py: Realized low-level spec: framework-decorated @data_type records (mutable dataclass exceptions with __str__ since frozen dataclasses are invalid for exceptions), @singleton_type/@operation protocol stubs for DAG, WaveScheduler, DAGRunner with no __initialize__.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Implemented concrete DAG (adjacency maps, duplicate/missing-node errors, DFS cycle detection, deterministic priority/lexicographic topological sort, roots/leaves, DP critical path), WaveScheduler (on-demand DAG resolution, state sync/promotion, priority waves, three failure policies, terminal detection), and DAGRunner (validate-first sequential waves, retries, per-node results, report with critical path) with auto-generated __initialize__ untouched.
[AUDIT] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: QA_AUDIT
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: [slug:dag_lite.dag.critical_path.longest_path] [viol:cov.missing_boundary_endpoint] Facet: empty graph critical path boundary Witness: missing_lines=[278] The contracted critical-path postconditions are unexercised for an empty registered graph: no assertion covers dag_lite.dag.critical_path.longest_path and dag_lite.dag.critical_path.cumulative_weight when zero nodes are registered, where the returned path sequence must be empty and the cumulative weight must be 0.0. The empty-graph boundary of these explicit postconditions lacks coverage.
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: [slug:dag_lite.scheduler.mark_failed.skip_downstream] [viol:cov.missing_branch] Facet: reconvergent dependent propagation Witness: missing_lines=[381] The transitive-dependent propagation required by dag_lite.scheduler.mark_failed.skip_downstream and dag_lite.scheduler.mark_failed.continue_on_error is unexercised for a reconvergent graph where two dependency paths from the failed node rejoin at a shared dependent. No assertion covers that shared dependent being transitioned once to SKIPPED while independent nodes stay eligible, so the diamond-shaped deduplication case of the contracted postconditions lacks coverage.
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: [slug:dag_lite.runner.run.sequential_waves] [viol:cov.missing_branch] Facet: unfinished wave loop halt Witness: missing_lines=[531] The contracted wave-loop halt condition is unexercised: no assertion covers a run where the scheduler reports unfinished work while no wave qualifies for dispatch, which occurs when a dependency edge is introduced on an already-ready node during execution, and run must terminate leaving the affected node non-terminal per dag_lite.runner.run.sequential_waves. This termination edge condition of the sequential-wave postcondition lacks coverage.
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: [slug:dag_lite.dag.topological_sort.dependency_order] [viol:cov.unreachable_under_spec] Facet: unreachable downstream in-degree guard Witness: missing_lines=[238] The skip branch for a downstream identifier lacking an in-degree entry is unreachable under the specification: dag_lite.dag.topological_sort.acyclic_graph and dag_lite.dag.validate.dependencies_exist require every referenced dependency to be registered before ordering, so every downstream adjacency value already owns an in-degree derived from the upstream mapping. Prune this span or annotate it with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: dependency existence and registration are guaranteed before ordering)'.
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: [slug:dag_lite.dag.critical_path.longest_path] [viol:cov.unreachable_under_spec] Facet: unreachable predecessor availability guard Witness: missing_lines=[291] The skip branch for an upstream dependency missing from the earliest-completion map is unreachable under the specification: dag_lite.dag.critical_path.longest_path computes the sweep over the topological ordering in which every prerequisite precedes its dependents, and missing dependencies were already rejected, so each dependency already holds an earliest completion entry when its dependent is processed. Prune this span or annotate it with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: topological order guarantees prerequisite completion values)'.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Addressed coverage feedback by pruning both unreachable guards: the downstream in-degree skip in topological_sort (dependency existence/registration guaranteed by _check_dependencies_exist before ordering) and the upstream earliest-completion skip in compute_critical_path (topological order guarantees every prerequisite holds a completion value).
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Addressed feedback: added empty-graph critical-path test (empty path, 0.0 weight), reconvergent diamond dependent tests for SKIP_DOWNSTREAM and CONTINUE_ON_ERROR (shared dependent skipped once, independent node stays eligible), and a runner wave-loop halt test where an execution-time edge on a ready node leaves unfinished nodes undispatchable so the run terminates without executing them.
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: [slug:dag_lite.runner.run.acyclic_graph] [viol:test.uncontracted_precondition] Facet: mid-run cyclic graph report expectation Witness: added_edge=b->c, cycle=c<->b, exp=DAGRunReport, obs=CycleError. This test's z-node action mutates the graph during wave execution by adding the edge b->c, making c depend on b while b already depends on c, so the graph contains the directed cycle c <-> b, yet the test expects run() to return a DAGRunReport with c and b left unexecuted; the low specification's dag_lite.runner.run.acyclic_graph precondition requires the graph to contain no directed cycles and designates CycleError as the contracted caller-violation outcome, so asserting a consolidated report for a cyclic graph asserts behavior for a violated precondition rather than a contracted postcondition. Because every node in an acyclic graph eventually becomes dispatchable, a halt scenario driven by an execution-time edge necessarily introduces a cycle and therefore cannot be asserted as a normal report-returning run.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Addressed feedback: removed the wave-loop halt test that mutated the graph mid-run into a cycle and asserted a consolidated DAGRunReport for a violated run.acyclic_graph precondition (CycleError is the only contracted outcome). Retained the empty-graph critical-path and reconvergent diamond dependent coverage; no unresolvable contracted scenario asserts report behavior for cyclic graphs.
