[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: [slug:dag_lite.runner.run.sequential_waves] [viol:cov.unexercisable_defensive_guard] Facet: wave loop stall guard Witness: missing_lines=[527] The empty-wave halt is a defensive stall guard that cannot execute under the specification closure: after dag_lite.runner.run.validate_before_waves validates the graph, the loop is driven solely by scheduler transitions over that validated graph, where a node reaches READY only when all of its dependencies are SUCCEEDED, an unfinished dag_lite.scheduler.is_finished result implies a READY or RUNNING node exists, and RUNNING nodes are always resolved within the same wave, so dag_lite.scheduler.next_wave always yields at least one node whenever the loop continues. Annotate this halt with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: a validated graph is not mutated while waves execute, so an unfinished scheduler always yields a non-empty wave)' instead of deleting the stall guard; the prior pruning of the two unreachable ordering guards did not address this remaining span.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Annotated the wave-loop empty-wave stall guard with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: a validated graph is not mutated while waves execute, so an unfinished scheduler always yields a non-empty wave)' rather than deleting it, resolving the unexercisable defensive guard feedback.
